export function instructionsHTML(fighters){return `<section><h3>1 · Move, jump and fight</h3><p>Be the last fighter standing. Choose a fighter and map, then Play Solo or create/join a room.</p><div class="help-columns"><div><h4>Keyboard & mouse</h4><dl><dt>A / D or ← / →</dt><dd>Move left / right.</dd><dt>Space, W or ↑</dt><dd>Jump. Tap again in the air to double jump.</dd><dt>X</dt><dd>Attack with automatic aim.</dd><dt>Mouse + left click</dt><dd>Aim and attack manually.</dd><dt>Z</dt><dd>Use your super move. It recharges in five seconds.</dd><dt>W / ↑ and S / ↓ near a vine</dt><dd>Climb up / down. Space jumps off.</dd><dt>L on Ocean Rafts</dt><dd>Hold to swim upward. Move with A/D; Space leaps out. Release L to dive.</dd><dt>R · F · Q</dt><dd>R activates a saved item. F uses it. Aim at a rival and Q commands your army.</dd><dt>Escape · H · Space during intro</dt><dd>Escape pauses solo play. H opens this guide. Space skips the cutscene.</dd></dl></div><div><h4>Phone / iPad</h4><p>Touch controls appear automatically. Use Touch On/Off in the header if needed.</p><ul><li>Drag the left thumb stick left/right to move, or up/down to climb vines.</li><li>Tap Jump twice for a double jump.</li><li>Hold Fire to attack. It aims at the nearest visible rival. Touch the arena to aim manually.</li><li>Tap Power to use Z. Its button shows the recharge countdown.</li><li>Item activates your selected reward; Use Item fires or attacks with it.</li><li>Army orders your allies. Hold Swim on the ocean map.</li><li>You can move, attack and jump with different fingers at the same time.</li><li>The small map shows fighters; your dot has a white outline. Portrait and landscape both work.</li></ul></div></div></section><section><h3>2 · All ${fighters.length} fighters & powers</h3><div class="help-powers">${fighters.map(f=>`<article style="border-color:${f.color}"><h4 style="color:${f.name==='SHADE'?'#cfd8e9':f.color}">${f.name} · ${f.power}</h4><p>${f.desc}</p><small>Z recharge: 5 seconds.</small></article>`).join('')}</div><p>Ivory has no gun: X punches, Z uppercuts, and Blaze cannot hurt him. His Fire Flower becomes five fire punches. Kobalt copies a rival for 14 seconds, then returns to his original form.</p></section><section><h3>3 · Lives, arenas and winning</h3><ul><li>Exactly five distinct fighters enter. In solo play, four are random bots. Every fighter starts with five lives.</li><li>Damage drains health and increases knockback. Armor absorbs damage first. A knockout or fall costs one life.</li><li>With lives left, you respawn after 1.2 seconds with full health and two seconds of protection. At zero lives, you are eliminated and spectate.</li><li>The danger zone begins closing after 18 seconds. Stay between its glowing borders or lose health.</li><li>The last fighter with lives left wins the trophy. Capturing everyone as allies does not end a match: they break free for a final showdown.</li><li>Classic, Desert, Deserted Island, Cloud Islands, Volcano, City and Ocean Rafts have different layouts. Avoid the lava on Volcano.</li><li>Only Ocean Rafts has swimming. After four seconds fully underwater, you start taking drowning damage. Swim up for air.</li><li>Green health pickups heal. Yellow lightning pickups temporarily speed up shooting.</li></ul><h4>Mystery blocks</h4><p>Jump into floating blocks from below. They recharge after seven seconds and cycle through three rewards:</p><ul><li><b>Grass:</b> random Wood, Iron, Diamond, Gold, Netherite, Wool, Emerald or Ruby armor. Armor is lost on respawn.</li><li><b>Ring:</b> 5–15 rings plus eight seconds of speed. Ring counts survive respawns.</li><li><b>Question:</b> Mini (70 HP), Super (140 HP) or Mega (200 HP), with matching size, for 12 seconds.</li></ul></section><section><h3>4 · Rewards & armies</h3><p>Human first-place wins award Fire Flower, then Super Star, then repeat. Rewards save in this browser; they do not sync between devices. Pick one in the lobby. It is spent only when R / Item activates it during a round.</p><ul><li><b>Fire Flower:</b> five small fireballs with F / Use Item. Aim with your mouse or arrow keys; touch auto-aims. Remaining shots survive respawns in that round. Ivory uses fire punches instead.</li><li><b>Super Star:</b> ten seconds of invincibility, once per round. F / Use Item attacks nearby rivals. It also protects against falls, the zone, lava and drowning.</li><li><b>Pixie & Rott:</b> touch rivals to recruit unicorn or zombie-dog allies. Aim at a rival, then Q / Army orders your team to attack. Allies cannot damage each other.</li><li><b>Shade:</b> Z creates a six-second aura. Nearby rivals entering it get ten seconds of near-black vision. Leaving and re-entering can blind them again. Shade and his allies keep their sight.</li></ul></section><section><h3>5 · Play with friends</h3><ol><li>Open the same public game on each device. No sign-in or app installation is needed.</li><li>Each person chooses a different fighter and enters a name.</li><li>One person chooses a map and taps Create Room.</li><li>Share the six-character room code. Friends enter it and tap Join Room.</li><li>The host starts when everyone is in. Rooms support two to five people; bots fill empty slots.</li></ol><p>Online matches cannot be paused. A disconnected fighter becomes a bot after a short timeout. Reconnection retries while the tab stays open; refreshing loses your room session. Return to the lobby to make a new room for another round.</p></section><section><h3>6 · Sound & menus</h3><p>Sound On/Off mutes all effects. Audio begins after a tap or keypress because browsers require that gesture. Watch Intro replays the cutscene; Space or Skip Intro skips it. This guide opens after the intro and can be reopened with How to Play or H. In online play, the match keeps running while this guide is open.</p></section>`;}
